            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/app/service.go store(): backoff starts at 1ms and doubles up to a 50ms cap. It waits only between tries, so 15 waits across 16 attempts total 513ms, which matches the comment and the bounded-latency tests. A lost race is bounded in both tries and time.",
              "engine/review/app/service.go Bind(): when AddWorktree fails, the code makes one extra Worktree inspection. It reuses the path only if err is nil, the worktree is present, belongs to the repository and is at the head. Otherwise it returns the original add error, so there is no retry loop and no masked failure. The Created flag is false for a worktree another bind made, which is correct.",
              "engine/review/app/service.go pause()/WithSleep: a nil sleep degrades to no waiting, which is the same behavior as the baseline. The diff does not show whether the command wires in a real sleep. That cannot be judged from this candidate, so it is not reported as a finding.",
              "Test changes in bind_test.go, fakes_test.go and record_test.go cover the new paths without real sleeps. The fake's worktreeLater indexing (count minus 2) correctly maps the second and later Worktree calls."
            ]
          }
        }
