            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Bind race recovery in engine/review/app/service.go: after a failed AddWorktree, isWorktreeAt re-inspects the path once. It requires err==nil, Present, OfRepository and Head==candidate head, and any other answer falls through to the original wrapped add error. AddWorktree is not retried. The new table test in engine/review/app/bind_test.go covers each rejecting state, including the error-with-plausible-state and partial-state cases, and asserts the add error is returned and not replaced by another sentinel.",
              "The fake Worktree sequencing in engine/review/app/fakes_test.go (first call uses the default answer, later calls use worktreeLater) matches what the new bind tests expect: inspected twice, one AddWorktree, Created false on reuse.",
              "Backoff in service.go store: no wait before the first try or after the last. Waits double from 1ms and cap at 50ms, so the 16-try worst case totals 513ms, which matches the comment. Tests in engine/review/app/record_test.go assert 16 Create calls, 16 listings, the error text, waits between tries only, monotonic and growing waits, per-wait and total bounds, and the nil-sleep path, all without real sleeping.",
              "The named-return removal in store is safe because every path returns explicit values.",
              "The wiring of WithSleep into the real command is not part of this candidate. Without it, New leaves sleep nil and production gets no backoff. I could not verify that wiring here, and the service's behavior with a nil sleep is tested."
            ]
          }
        }
